      "title": "Admission Counselor/ Assistant Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nLebanon Valley College is seeking an enthusiastic and relationship-focused Admission Counselor / Assistant Director to join our Admission team. This full-time position plays an important role in building LVC’s enrollment pipeline and serves as one of the College’s first points of contact for prospective students and families. The successful candidate will be an engaging ambassador for LVC who enjoys connecting with students, traveling, building relationships, and sharing the value of an LVC education. This position will manage an assigned recruitment territory, evaluate admission applications, conduct presentations and interviews, and guide prospective students and families throughout the admission process. Qualifications include a bachelor’s degree, at least one year of successful experience in a related field, preferably in higher education, excellent communication, interpersonal, organizational, and customer service skills, the ability to build relationships, influence others, achieve goals, and manage multiple priorities, proficiency with Microsoft Office, CRM systems (Salesforce preferred), and social media, a valid driver’s license and the ability to travel regionally. The availability for evening and weekend responsibilities is required as needed. Bilingual proficiency is preferred but not required. If you are energized by helping students discover their potential and want to play a meaningful role in shaping the future of LVC, please submit a letter of interest, resume and the contact information for three professional references to ADP. The position will remain open until filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c6864f58-380f-4d35-a085-a83ec5fb3f0b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207298495563_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director of the MBA Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nLebanon Valley College invites applications for a renewable-term faculty appointment as Director of Graduate Programs in Business, beginning Fall 2027. This 9-month faculty appointment combines graduate program administration with faculty teaching responsibilities and will include a 12-month administrative stipend associated with graduate program leadership responsibilities. The Director will provide academic and strategic leadership for the department’s online graduate programs, advancing program quality, enrollment growth, student retention, innovation, and regional engagement. Responsibilities include graduate curriculum development, assessment and ACBSP accreditation reporting, faculty mentoring and support, course scheduling, student advising, recruitment initiatives, partnership development, and collaboration with other academic departments. Teaching assignments and workload expectations will be established in consultation with department and academic leadership, taking into consideration administrative responsibilities and departmental needs. Graduate courses are delivered exclusively online to serve working professionals and geographically diverse student populations. Regular on-campus availability is expected for departmental meetings, faculty collaboration, and student and adjunct support. Candidates must demonstrate graduate-level teaching experience, substantive experience with online instruction, and a strong understanding of adult learners, graduate advising, and effective instructional practices. Excellent communication, organizational, and collaborative skills are essential. Teaching experience in data analytics is highly preferred. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to academic excellence, student success, program innovation, and Lebanon Valley College’s mission and values. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, separate statements of teaching philosophy, research interests, curriculum vitae, and complete contact information for three professional references through ADP. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary and faculty rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c6864f58-380f-4d35-a085-a83ec5fb3f0b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207298489007_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Payroll Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nLebanon Valley College is seeking a detail-oriented, service-focused payroll coordinator to manage payroll processing for college employees, including monthly, biweekly, and student payrolls. This position is responsible for ensuring accurate and timely payroll processing, maintaining compliance with applicable tax regulations and College policies, researching, and resolving payroll discrepancies, and supporting related student employment processes. The payroll coordinator works collaboratively with Human Resources, the Business Office, and other campus partners while maintaining the highest standards of confidentiality and customer service. Preferred qualifications include a bachelor’s degree or some college coursework, a minimum of five years of payroll experience with higher education experience a plus, knowledge of ADP payroll software and Microsoft Office applications, strong attention to detail, strong organizational and communication skills, the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines, and a demonstrated commitment to confidentiality, collaboration, and exceptional customer service. The successful candidate will support Lebanon Valley College’s mission and values and contribute to a culture of belonging and legendary service through the College’s ASPIRE standards. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, resume and the contact information for three professional references to ADP. The position will remain open until filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
      "department": ""
