      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nThe Lebanon Valley College Department of Social Sciences invites applications for the position of assistant professor of Criminal Justice. This is a full-time, nine-month, three-year renewable appointment, beginning in August 2027. Responsibilities include teaching a broad variety of undergraduate courses in criminal justice and criminology such as Introduction to Criminal Justice, Police and Society, Corrections, Offender and Prisoner Rights, Crime and Public Policy, senior seminar, as well as developing other classes that meet the evolving needs of students and the department. Candidates should have an excellent record of teaching and a demonstrated ability to teach at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will possess a Ph.D. in Criminal Justice or a closely related field such as Public Administration with a concentration in CJ. A doctorate must be completed before the starting date. Additional responsibilities include maintaining regular on campus office hours, attending faculty and department meetings, advising, and assisting in the recruiting and retention of students.  Interested applicants should submit; (1) cover letter addressing teaching experience, philosophy, and ability to meet job requirements (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) three professional references with current contact information. Please submit all materials through ADP. Review of candidate materials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
      "department": ""
