      "title": "Student Affairs Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nLebanon Valley College is seeking a highly organized, collaborative, and student-focused professional to serve as a student affairs assistant within the Center for Student Engagement (CSE). This position provides essential administrative and operational support to the Offices of Student Engagement, Spiritual Life, Culture, Community, & Belonging, and Service & Community Engagement, while also providing backup administrative support to other areas within Student Affairs as needed. As a key member of the CSE team, the Student Affairs Assistant serves as a welcoming first point of contact for students, families, employees, and campus visitors. The position helps ensure the smooth day-to-day operation of the Center while supporting programs, events, communications, budgets, scheduling, student employment, and departmental systems. The successful candidate will bring exceptional customer service, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, discretion, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, student-centered environment. Qualifications include a high school diploma or equivalent, administrative or office support experience, strong organizational skills and attention to detail, excellent interpersonal and customer service skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work effectively in a busy, student-centered environment. Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, resume and the contact information for three professional references to ADP. The position will remain open until filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
      "department": ""
