    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c6864f58-380f-4d35-a085-a83ec5fb3f0b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207104391538_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Asst Director of Alumni & Family Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nThe Lebanon Valley College Office of Advancement seeks an assistant director of alumni & family engagement. The assistant director coordinates and manages activities related to expanding the College's network of alumni, current families and other supporters. The assistant director plans and executes opportunities (both in-person and virtually) to form strong connections between the institution and student families, from enrollment through graduation, and beyond. While reporting to the director of alumni & family engagement, the assistant director collaborates often with Development colleagues to implement programs, strategies, and charitable gift requests that support the College's comprehensive fundraising campaign. Qualifications include a bachelor's degree, 1 —2 years relevant higher education, or not-for-profit engagement or experience, a valid PA driver's license and, availability for significant evening or weekend hours, and travel as necessary. The successful candidate should thrive being a part of a dynamic team but also work very well independently. Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, resume, and contact information for three professional references to ADP. The review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to excellence through its employment practices and welcomes applicants with exceptional qualifications, particularly those with demonstrable commitments to a more inclusive society and world. The College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse student body, faculty and staff and promotes a culture of accountability, student centeredness, professionalism, inclusiveness, respect, and empowerment.",
