    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c6864f58-380f-4d35-a085-a83ec5fb3f0b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207043560578_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Production",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nThe Lebanon Valley College Department of Music invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Production. This is a full-time, nine-month, three-year renewable contract position, beginning in August 2027. Qualified candidates must have contemporary professional experience in any of the following: Studio Recording, DAW Production, Mixing, Mastering, Immersive Audio, Electronic Music, Sound Design, and/or Live Sound. The position requires a master’s degree or equivalent professional experience. Previous teaching experience is highly preferred. The position’s duties include assisting in the maintenance of on-campus studios, teaching 12 credits per semester, participation in various committees and student advising, and aiding in the recruitment and retainment of exceptional students.  Lebanon Valley College will be renovating and upgrading our main performance venue into a state-of-the-art concert hall with active acoustics and spatial audio capabilities. Music Production faculty and students will be afforded the opportunity to explore and utilize object-based mixing and immersive audio technologies through this new facility. Applicants should submit: (1) cover letter addressing professional experience, interest in teaching, and ability to meet job requirements; (2) curriculum vitae/resume; and (3) three professional references with current contact information. Former teaching evaluations, portfolios, and letters of recommendation are accepted but not required. Please submit all materials through ADP. Review of candidate materials will begin October 31st and continue until the position is filled.  Lebanon Valley College is committed to excellence through its employment practices and welcomes applicants with exceptional qualifications, particularly those with demonstrable commitments to a more inclusive society and world. The College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse student body, faculty and staff and promotes a culture of accountability, student centeredness, professionalism, inclusiveness, respect, and empowerment.",
