    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c6864f58-380f-4d35-a085-a83ec5fb3f0b&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9206853981283_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Inst. in Design, Media and Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nLebanon Valley College’s Design, Media & Technology Department invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach two hands-on sections of the class  MIS for Competitive Advantage . The successful candidate will teach two sections of DIGI 263: MIS for Competitive Advantage to begin January 2027. This class meets in person, on campus, on Tuesdays and Wednesdays from 6:30 p.m. to 9:30 p.m. This course explores how organizations use and integrate technology in their business operations. An emphasis is placed on understanding and applying the business models and strategies that support technology and business decisions. Qualified candidates should hold a master’s degree in a relevant field or possess significant professional experience in business or a related area. The ideal candidate will demonstrate substantial experience in MIS. Prior teaching experience is preferred, along with a demonstrated commitment to applied, experiential learning. Applicants should submit a  brief cover letter detailing their teaching and professional experience, a current CV or résumé  (including email address and phone number), and contact information for three professional references to ADP. A review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
