      "title": "Asst/Assoc Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\n\nLocation: Annville\n\nPosition Opening: Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting The Department of Business, Accounting, and Economics at Lebanon Valley College invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, 3-year renewable term, assistant/associate professor of accounting starting in January 2027. The assistant professor is responsible for teaching a standard academic course load as assigned. The successful candidate will have a master’s degree with five or more years of accounting experience. CPA is strongly preferred. Qualifications to teach courses in Financial and Intermediate Accounting, Auditing, and other courses in related fields and disciplines are also highly desirable. Familiarity in ACBSP business school accreditation standards via a commitment to the assessment of learning outcomes is preferred.  More information about the department can be found at https://www.lvc.edu/majors-program/business-administration/ .  Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and the contact information for three professional references through ADP. Review of candidate materials will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lebanon Valley College is committed to fostering excellence through diversity in its educational programs and employment practices. The College welcomes applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those who have demonstrated a commitment to creating a more inclusive society and world.",
